 WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS (the specification)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Source : web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/ChargeStatusWidget.tsx (read end-to-end)
 Hooks  : useVehicles, useVehicleState(id), useUnits (unitPrefs.distance), useTranslation('dashboard')
 Render branches (all reproduced):
   1. state.is_charging → grid of four metrics:
        Power        = fmtNumber(charger_power) kW          (global precision, default 2)
        Rate         = fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI(charge_rate ?? 0, unit)) {unit}/h
        Battery      = {battery_level}%
        Time to Full = time_to_full_charge > 0 ? fmtNumber(_,1)+"h" : "—"
   2. state (not charging) → "Not Charging" +
        {battery_level}% · {fmtNumber(convertDistanceFromSI(rated_range ?? 0, unit), 0)} {unit}
   3. else (no state) → EmptyState "No charge data"
 SI-floor: charge_rate (m·h⁻¹) and rated_range (m) arrive SI; converted at the
           display boundary via convertDistanceFromSI — NIST factors km/mi/ft.
 i18n keys extracted : Charging, Power, Rate, Battery, Time to Full, Not Charging, No charge data
 Registry (registry/charging.ts → "charge-status"):
   id=charge-status  category=charging  default 2×2  min 1×2  max 3×40

